  {
   "id": "dd3uFCRuwbAJ",
   "from": "Bill Shobe",
   "author": "05876d7dccb66035",
   "date": "2014-01-03T18:33:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: Shiny version ' 0.0.0 ' found. Shiny Server requires at least ' 0.7.0 '.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I had the same problem. I followed the recommended steps and still had the same result. After much trial and error (I am a rank amateur in Linux), I made Shiny Server work. The problem I was having was that some of the essential R packages needed to make Shiny Server work were out of date. I suggest that you follow the instructions at the link recommended, but add a couple of steps. After installing R, install the R development tools:<div><br></div><div><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Courier;background-color:rgb(245,243,191)\">sudo apt-get install r-base-dev</p><div><br></div><div>Then, update all of your R packages (codetools is particularly critical, I think):</div><div><br></div><div><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Courier;background-color:rgb(245,243,191)\">sudo su -  -c &quot;R -e \\&quot;update.packages(ask=FALSE,checkBuilt=TRUE,repos=&#39;<a href=\"http://watson.nci.nih.gov/cran_mirror/&#39;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://watson.nci.nih.gov/cran_mirror/&#39;&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405392217000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3WwSXPl_rSQOl4JMupCUzS\">http://watson.nci.nih.gov/cran_mirror/&#39;</a>)\\&quot;&quot;</p></div><div><br></div>Next, follow the remaining instructions to install the shiny package as instructed, and the shiny-server. Once I did this, I copied the examples directory &#39;01_hello&#39; into the /srv/shiny-server directory. </div><div><br></div><div>After adding these additional steps to the instructions on the Shiny Server website, my instance worked.</div><div><br></div><div>I hope this helps.</div><div></div></div>"
    ],
